---
source: tests/attestation_state.rs
description: "The attestation state that lives on the localnet once e2e/run.sh has run, on attestations-v2. For each subject: how many registry events name it, and the attestations at its address, derived off-chain from the registry and subject ids, split into live and revoked by `revoked_at_ms`, with their data and rendered Display; then every registry event, in order. Ids are replaced with names: a package's directory name, `name@vN` for version N of an upgraded package, or a label from the test. A line starting with `!!` marks an inconsistency."
---
